[{"text":"FVD[p, mu] is the D-dimensional vector p with Lorentz index mu.","anchor":"fvd"},{"text":"Overview, FCE, FCI, FV, Pair.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"FVD[p, \\[Mu]]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[p^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FVD[p - q, \\[Mu]]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[(p-q)^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FVD[p, \\[Mu]] // StandardForm (*FVD[p, \\[Mu]]*)","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCI[FVD[p, \\[Mu]]] // StandardForm (*Pair[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu], D], Momentum[p, D]]*)","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"There is no special function to expand momenta in FVD.","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ex = ExpandScalarProduct[FVD[p - q, \\[Mu]]]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[p^{\\mu }-q^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ex // StandardForm (*Pair[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu], D], Momentum[p, D]] - Pair[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu], D], Momentum[q, D]]*)","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"}]